From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Hunter Laux <hunterlaux@gmail.com>
Date: Tue, 17 Nov 2026 01:42:14 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] ad5x: A/B main OS slots, safe mode, all of the RAM
 (prototype)

U-Boot's boot rules for a main OS in both slots: the flagged slot (7.3,
then 6.6), the other slot (the flag moved there), Kiln OS 1.x's recovery
OS in slot A where it still is, then safe mode (ad5x.safe=1, watchdog
off; twice unfinished: the prompt). A slot holds the main OS when its
rootfs has Kiln's kernels. State records the slot and safe mode, failure
records are per slot (1.x's names stay slot B's).

The kernel gets all of the RAM: mem=256M@0x0 (and the X2600H's second
bank), no rmem=/rtos_size= holes, lpj as the 2025 stock SPL passes it.

Signed-off-by: Hunter Laux <hunterlaux@gmail.com>
---
 arch/mips/mach-jz47xx/x2600/spl.c |  10 +-
 board/flashforge/ad5x/ad5x.c      | 145 ++++++++++----
 board/flashforge/ad5x/bootlogic.c | 313 +++++++++++++++++++-----------
 board/flashforge/ad5x/bootlogic.h |  42 +++-
 4 files changed, 341 insertions(+), 169 deletions(-)

diff --git a/arch/mips/mach-jz47xx/x2600/spl.c b/arch/mips/mach-jz47xx/x2600/spl.c
